  "solution": "The logic followed here is:\n\nLogic: **(2nd number × 2) - 1st number = 3rd number**.\n\n(32, 70, 108) \n\n→ (70 × 2) - 32 \n\n⇒ 140 - 32 = 108.\n\nNow, checking the options:\n\nOption 1: (44, 82, 124)\n\n→ (82 × 2) - 44 \n\n⇒ 164 - 44 = 120 ≠ 124.\n\nOption 2: (34, 72, 122)\n\n→ (72 × 2) - 34 \n\n⇒ 144 - 34 = 110 ≠ 122.\n\n**Option 3: (42, 80, 118) **\n\n**→ (80 × 2) - 42 **\n\n**⇒ 160 - 42 = 118 = 118.**\n\nOption 4: (38, 76, 116)\n\n→ (76 × 2) - 38 \n\n⇒ 152 - 38 = 114 ≠ 116.\n\nHence, the correct answer is **\"Option 3\"**.",
